    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -680,
        "y": -300
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Kingma and Ba, \"Adam: A Method for Stochastic Optimization\", ICLR 2015. Claim: Adam's per-parameter step sizes, built from running averages of the gradient and of its square, reach a lower training loss in the same number of steps than SGD with or without momentum. Recipe: three copies of one 784-256-256-10 ReLU MLP on 10,000 MNIST images, batch 128, 5 epochs, trained with SGD lr 0.01, SGD lr 0.01 with momentum 0.9, and Adam lr 0.001 (the paper's default). Under seed 0 on a CPU the final training losses are 0.79 for SGD, 0.27 for SGD with momentum and 0.21 for Adam.\n\nKingma 與 Ba，〈Adam: A Method for Stochastic Optimization〉，ICLR 2015。論點：Adam 用梯度和梯度平方的移動平均，替每個參數各自決定步長，同樣步數下能把訓練損失降得比有無 momentum 的 SGD 都低。配方：同一個 784-256-256-10 ReLU MLP 複製三份，在 10,000 張 MNIST 影像上以 batch 128 訓練 5 個 epoch，分別用 SGD lr 0.01、SGD lr 0.01 加 momentum 0.9，以及 Adam lr 0.001（論文的預設值）。在 CPU 上以種子 0 執行，最後的訓練損失是 SGD 0.79、SGD 加 momentum 0.27、Adam 0.21。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "start",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -420,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 360
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-data",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 1000,
        "y": -300
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "MNIST ships with the repository under backend/data, so the run reads it from disk. DatasetSplit keeps a fixed 10,000 of the 60,000 training images; its own seed (0) picks them, so every arm trains on the same images through the one DataLoader.\n\nMNIST 隨專案放在 backend/data 底下，執行時直接從磁碟讀取。DatasetSplit 從 60,000 張訓練影像中固定留下 10,000 張，挑哪幾張由它自己的種子（0）決定，所以每一組都透過同一個 DataLoader 在同一批影像上訓練。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "dl-train",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 320,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-arms",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -300,
        "y": 400
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Each arm has its own SequentialModel node with the same layers. One model node wired into three TrainingLoops would hand every loop the same weights, and each loop would continue from what the previous one left. The run seed (0, stored in the file) fixes the shuffle order, any dropout masks and each model's initial weights. Every node is seeded from the run seed and its own id, so the arms start from different draws of the same initialisation. With Persist weights between runs on (Settings > Training Behavior), a second Run continues from the trained weights; turn it off to repeat these numbers.\n\n每一組都有自己的 SequentialModel 節點，圖層完全相同。如果一個模型節點同時接到三個 TrainingLoop，每個迴圈拿到的是同一份權重，後跑的會接著前一個留下的結果繼續訓練。執行種子（0，存在檔案裡）固定了洗牌順序、dropout 遮罩和每個模型的初始權重。每個節點的種子由執行種子和節點自己的 id 推得，所以各組的初始權重是同一種初始化方式下的不同抽樣。在設定 > 訓練行為中開啟「在多次執行間保留權重」時，第二次執行會從訓練過的權重繼續；關閉它才能重現這些數字。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "model-sgd",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -340,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-adam",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 360,
        "y": 2740
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Adam's betas 0.9, 0.999 and eps 1e-8 are the values in the paper's Algorithm 1. The first epoch shows the difference most clearly: Adam's average loss is 0.80 against 2.20 for plain SGD. The paper also compares AdaGrad and RMSProp; set an Optimizer's type to Adagrad or RMSprop to add them.\n\nAdam 的 betas 0.9、0.999 與 eps 1e-8 都是論文演算法 1 裡的值。第一個 epoch 的差距最明顯：Adam 的平均損失是 0.80，純 SGD 是 2.20。論文也比較了 AdaGrad 和 RMSProp；把某個 Optimizer 的 type 改成 Adagrad 或 RMSprop 就能加進來比較。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "opt-adam",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 340
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    }
  ],
